WEBVTT

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:04.050
All of you here at 
Agricultural University!

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.730
Hello! I'm Tanaka Kyoko!

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.730
Hello!

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:12.070
Tanaka Kyoko-chan at the Agricultural University

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.830
This is my first time here,

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.050
and wow, it's so big!

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:19.120
Staff Only

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.550
I couldn't believe it!

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.070
So you do all kinds of 
research here, huh?

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.600
I even had a chance to take part in some

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.540
of the research being done here
that I didn't understand.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.100
But I really appreciate it!

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.550
Miss Agricultural University's Bar
Aoi's Bar

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.540
All right, here are your 
three pineapple pulques.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:36.220
Thanks.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.820
Thank you very much!

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.430
Looks like Tanaka Kyoko's 
show has started.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.770
We'll be done for the day soon.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.240
Sawaki-kun, that was the last 
of the pineapple pulque, right?

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:47.940
Yes.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.490
Then let's sell out the rest, too!

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:51.570
Okay!

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:52.690
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.100
What can I get for you?

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.950
Aya-chan totally bailed us out!

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.450
Please have 
exact change 
ready.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.450
50 yen coins 
are annoying, 
so pineapple 
and guava 
flavoring will 
cost 100 yen.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:57.710
She's really streamlined our methods

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:59.450
of giving change and running the stall.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.060
I even feel like it's easier 
to work in the back,

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:03.180
No longer offering 
trays since collecting them is a pain.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:03.690
knowing what's going on up front.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.540
Thank you very much.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:09.170
But, you know, you guys have no focus

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:10.710
without the princess here.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.130
Thank you! I love you all!

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.610
Kyoko!

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.260
Thank you, too!

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.710
Well, I'll be going now.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:27.390
I have to be a ring girl during 
the nighttime harvest festival.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:29.890
It's that late already?

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.910
The nighttime harvest festival?

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:34.270
It'll be tough without you,

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:36.390
but you sure saved us. Thanks.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.870
I'll go check it out later.

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:40.960
Aya-san, can you come 
help us again tomorrow?

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.580
It's the princess who 
should be here, not me.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.100
Why don't you go look for her?

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:51.500
I think she kind of 
likes to feel needed.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.560
We don't have anything to brew!

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.010
Give us something!

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:03.470
Moyashimon

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.470
Returns

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.360
<i>All scheduled events for day one of</i>

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.940
<i>the harvest festival 
have come to a close.</i>

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:38.980
No 
Climbing

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:38.980
78th Annual University Harvest Festival

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:33.970
<i>The gate is now closing.</i>

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:37.800
<i>We will open again tomorrow 
morning at 10 o'clock.</i>

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:51.790
Professor Itsuki?

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.920
I wonder if he was at Kei's place.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:04.800
It's ringing more than usual...

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:08.560
That's the signal to start the 
nighttime harvest festival.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:09.430
Nighttime Harvest Festival

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:09.430
Event Information

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.430
Smooth vs. Chunky

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:10.430
The Bean Paste Battle

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:11.680
Associate Professor Tachibana vs. Professor Mikami

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:11.680
Prof. Mikami Will Accept All of Tachibana's Rules

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:11.680
At the Special Ring in the University Baseball Field

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.930
The daytime harvest festival is 
for interacting with the locals.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:16.190
The festival as seen on the outside.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:19.260
But the school's fundamental 
principle is "self-sufficiency."

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:22.190
Its true face is revealed 
after the gate is closed.

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:25.440
I heard something like 
that in spring, too.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:28.930
The thing with Professor Mikami 
that Aya-chan is involved with

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.950
looks the most interesting.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.830
I seriously can't believe you guys!

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.020
If Aya-san hadn't shown up,

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:38.840
the three of us would've started 
throwing punches and I'd be dead!

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:42.430
Oh, Hasegawa never turned up?

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:43.840
I wonder what she's up to, and where.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.690
What's this jar?

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:49.600
It'd better not be something 
pre-chewed again.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.100
I'm not selling the pre-chewed 
stuff this time.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:56.480
By the way, "pre-chewed" means...

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.820
You chew up rice and spit it out,

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:03.320
then add water to mix the rice 
with enzymes in the saliva,

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:07.010
so the starch in the rice is oxidized...

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:09.490
In other words, it's sake made by 
chewing the ingredients first.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:13.320
I thought you were planning to 
sell it at Aoi's Bar tomorrow.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:14.620
Don't be stupid!

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.610
This is the pulque for tomorrow.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:19.630
That makes sense.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.920
Is this what you used to suck it out?

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.630
Like this?

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.260
Ah, it's all done.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:34.770
Please be there to help tomorrow, okay?

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:42.020
I wonder if Hasegawa-san 
caught a cold...

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:47.660
If you'll excuse me.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:00.260
You know, the Hotel Ritz 
here used to be a palace.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.370
They say one of its

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:05.050
owners was Napoleon's favorite jeweler.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.860
Five of the largest jewelers in the world, 
known as the grand cinq,

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:11.570
can be found in the Place Vendôme 
in front of the hotel.

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:15.780
Want to take a break then 
go out and buy a ring?

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:20.500
Thank you all for waiting.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:24.650
It's now time for our main event!

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.170
Now, entering the ring in search 
of revenge for the fifth time,

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.660
Associate Professor Tachibana!

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:34.580
Tachibana!

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:35.910
Come on, win!

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.620
You want to be a professor, don't you?

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.160
Associate professor forever!

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.970
To become a professor 
at this university,

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:43.850
you need the approval of 
all current professors

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:46.420
at an annual professors' meeting.

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.870
But associate professors have a chance

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:51.430
for revenge at the nighttime 
harvest festival.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.700
They can fight with the professors

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:55.210
that vetoed them at the meeting,

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.180
and if they win, 
they can become professors.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.180
I Wanna Be a Professor

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.110
Doesn't Mr. Tachibana ever think

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:01.190
Tachibana

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:01.190
of fighting back through his studies?

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:05.040
Nah, rumor has it, Professor 
Mikami doesn't approve him

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.960
just because he enjoys these fights.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:11.990
Yuuki 
Liquors

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:11.990
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.620
As harsh as ever, I see!

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:25.250
You said your name is Hasegawa-kun?

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.140
What's the matter?

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:30.010
W-Well...

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:33.760
Hasegawa-sama, shall I pour for you?

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.140
Please.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.390
Here I am, Mikami!

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:53.530
This is my fifth year in this ring!

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.080
This time, I'm taking you down!

00:07:56.310 --> 00:08:00.410
Entering the ring next 
is Professor Mikami!

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.880
Mikami!

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:05.170
You copied my thesis at the 
last conference, didn't you?!

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:06.920
Last Year

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:08.800
Professor Mikami has used Qigong

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:12.420
to defeat Mr. Tachibana 
for the past four years.

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:17.060
But Professor Mikami's 
getting on in years, too.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:19.760
He was in the hospital 
since this past spring,

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:22.180
so this is the perfect 
chance for Mr. Tachibana.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.080
By the way, Professor Mikami has

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:28.690
fully accepted Mr. Tachibana's KO rules,

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.180
and left only the words 
"Kill Tachibana" behind

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:32.820
and has been hospitalized 
up until last week.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.700
Also, before he was hospitalized,

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.450
he became the adviser of the

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:38.950
agricultural society's 
cyber technology club!

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:45.460
Live from the hospital

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:45.460
Hello, Mikami here.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:00.720
What the hell?

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:03.270
Professor Mikami launches his 
explosive Professor Genocide move!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:04.690
Seventeen hit combo!

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.730
Tachibana has been in 
the air the whole time!

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:14.490
Goodbye.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:19.620
Hasegawa-sama.

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:22.890
This will be your key.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:26.290
From now on, you can just 
put this in that hole,

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.880
and the door will open from the outside.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:31.450
What is this farce?

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:34.090
I took time out of my schedule 
because the vice president

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:35.250
called me here...

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:36.710
It's forbidden to speak of

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:39.850
who comes here and what happens inside.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:40.970
That's our rule.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.250
I don't get it.

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.230
Those men in the bar were

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:51.400
central figures in Japan's 
political and business circles.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:55.660
Why was Professor Itsuki 
sitting with them?

00:09:55.660 --> 00:10:00.190
And they were all talking about 
Haruka, Haruka, Haruka...

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:05.910
Hello?

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.110
It's me.

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:09.420
Oh! You were just at the...

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:12.230
Bad move, Hasegawa-kun.

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:15.700
We live in a world where you never 
know who might be listening,

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.300
even if you're talking to yourself.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:18.680
Wiretap-kun

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:28.690
When you're past 60 like me, 
a man like him is just a boy.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.260
Was that good enough, Itsuki-san?

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:34.620
Yes. Thank you.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:35.940
You've been a big help.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.020
Don't mention it.

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:40.500
You're a member here, after all.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:45.910
But only you would call us all together

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.840
over something like this, Keizou.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:49.210
I love it.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.450
He's gone home.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:54.460
Ah, thank you.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:57.460
A wedding in France, eh?

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.680
It would be wonderful,

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:02.000
if only it was what she really wanted.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:08.180
Day Two

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:08.310
It's day two of the harvest festival!

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:12.400
Fried Chicken

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:12.460
Live Demo

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:12.460
You all love it, right?

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:16.010
Keep frying it up! The kids are waiting!

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:21.800
Wait just a bit, okay?

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:23.620
We're going to make some 
delicious fried chicken.

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:26.300
Both meat and vegetables 
are raised to eat!

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:28.490
That's our university's motto.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:31.070
Fried chicken comes in 
exchange for a life.

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:34.070
Parents and children, 
be sure to watch closely!

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:36.130
What?

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.850
Getting married in France?

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:42.200
So Haruka-san is actually quitting school?

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.140
When did it come to this?

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:47.400
But it was her father's decision, right?

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:49.890
Is she really okay with it?

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:53.130
Then Professor Itsuki said,

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:59.400
"Either way... France, 
eh? I wish I could go."

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.490
Either way?

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:02.840
To get her back?

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:04.410
To attend the wedding, I'd say.

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:09.560
Maybe she just never mentioned 
her marriage to us?

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:11.820
I doubt that.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:15.700
Haruka-san once said she would 
stay at this school forever.

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:19.850
So I don't think she really 
wants this marriage...

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:23.180
But what can we do?

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:26.400
Aya-san said we should go look for her,

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.180
but France is pretty far away.

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:31.370
Why even ask what we can do?

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:33.080
Would a woman like Hasegawa

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:36.190
even want guys like us to bring her back?

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:39.710
First of all, how much do you 
think plane tickets cost?

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:41.440
Who here has that kind of money?

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.200
Hey, the customers will be here soon.

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:52.960
What are you gonna do, Kei?

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:54.550
Head back?

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:55.950
I haven't been here in a while.

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:57.580
Anything I can help with?

00:12:57.850 --> 00:13:01.570
I think it's time for 
me to do my part here.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.010
We are Aoi's Bar!

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.350
Cosplay photo ops for 1,000 yen!

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:14.350
We'll throw in a smile for 
an additional 200 yen!

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.350
Have some pulque before you go, too!

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:19.870
Hey, goth lolita girl, 
link arms with the bunny girl!

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:21.320
Okay!

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:23.280
How's this?

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:26.360
No running off without paying!

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.320
Oikawa, stop that!

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:30.160
And Yuuki-kun, don't follow her!

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:32.260
What are they thinking?!

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:34.250
There's no end to all these customers!

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:36.170
We need something to brew!

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:38.020
Okay, okay...

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.910
Hey, which one of you is Aoi-chan?

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:46.020
Neither of us is Aoi-chan.

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:48.550
Aoi-chan is the mistress of this bar.

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:50.930
Right, ma'am?

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:56.430
I'll go look for something, too!

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:57.480
Please, stop!

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:58.940
I won't lose to you brats!

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:58.940
Don't go overboard!

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:02.570
You're glowing, Aoi!

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.440
Irresistible!

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:08.320
Why is this the only one you had?

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:11.310
Sold Out

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:11.330
There's a planetarium set up

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.990
at the entry arch until seven tonight,

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.110
so the school is open to 
the public until then.

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:17.830
After that is the last night event.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:22.110
How much did we earn 
together with the stall?

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:25.050
Enough to send at least one 
person to France, I think.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:26.290
No way!

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:28.470
That's what you two were thinking?

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:31.730
I wouldn't dress like this otherwise.

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:33.280
Excuse me...

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:35.130
Could we take your picture?

00:14:35.130 --> 00:14:36.480
Sure!

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:00.220
Did you make lots of money?

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.300
Uh... yes.

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:06.800
We nearly sold out of all we 
had prepared this morning.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.930
Misato-san and the others 
said we should keep

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.300
the money in here.

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:13.440
I see.

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:22.980
Haruka's not coming...

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.960
male          female

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.810
What happened to her?

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:31.880
We could compete much 
better if she was here.

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:33.370
Yeah.

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:47.320
Hasegawa-san has some unfinished 
research, doesn't she?

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:50.280
Quite a lot of it.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:52.630
She's been in my seminar 
for a long time.

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:24.670
The final event should be 
starting right about now.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.670
What? There's still more to do?

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:30.920
Last night's event was authorized.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:34.320
We're about to join in the 
unauthorized nighttime festival.

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:35.430
Wear shoes inside

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:38.930
I'm really tired, so I think 
I'll sleep a little...

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.170
What the hell for?

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:42.810
This is when the real deal starts!

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:47.540
The student-run dorm 
resistance movement!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:50.150
You guys are the main 
attraction this year.

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:51.940
We're looking forward to good results!

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:55.390
I hear 4,500 yen from No. 53!

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:56.890
5,000 for No. 24!

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:57.880
Any others?

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:00.930
Exhibitors                                        Auctioneer

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:00.380
The photo with a glimpse 
of tennis club member

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:02.700
Haruna's bra is sold to 
No. 24 for 5,000 yen!

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.230
Yes!

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:06.040
An auction hall!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:08.480
Everyone sells the treasures 
they've collected

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.090
over the past year.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:12.090
It's our turn.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:13.470
Get ready quick.

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:14.950
Exhibitors                              Auctioneer

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:16.720
And now for this year's main attraction!

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:18.470
Pre-chewed Sake

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:20.720
This is steamed and crushed

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:23.020
sake brewing rice from this year's crop.

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:24.980
Also, take a look at the screen.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:27.230
Pre-chewed Sake

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:28.090
In the Waiting Room

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:32.790
We might start selling 
this around school soon.

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:35.990
It whitens skin through 
the power of enzymes.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.320
Wow, that sounds great!

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.250
Hm? It tastes like regular gum.

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:49.280
It is regular gum.

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.750
It's what's in it that's amazing.

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:55.020
You can spit it out in this.

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:57.110
Oh, thank you.

00:18:11.970 --> 00:18:14.530
Kyoko-san, it's time to go on standby.

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:16.760
Okay, lead the way.

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:19.320
Thank you for assisting 
the biology department.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.620
We'll be going.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:23.490
Pre-chewed sake made with the saliva

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:26.120
of this year's harvest festival 
concert guest, Tanaka Kyoko,

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:27.770
starts at 5,000 yen!

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:28.640
6,000 yen!

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:29.690
8,000!

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:30.230
11,000!

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:31.770
14,000!

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:33.650
20,000!

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.130
H-How about 30,000?!

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:42.930
Planetarium

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:48.090
<i>The stars Vega and Altair are 
part of the Summer Triangle.</i>

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:52.000
<i>As mentioned previously, 
the role of the North Star</i>

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.770
<i>has been gradually 
transferred to other stars.</i>

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:56.920
<i>In about 12,000 years, these two stars,</i>

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:58.920
<i>also called Orihime and Hikoboshi,</i>

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:01.620
80,000 yen, huh?

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:01.620
<i>will rule the night sky 
as the North Star.</i>

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:05.120
Can we say that's good?

00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:07.960
Well, it should be enough 
to cover the food stall.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.540
I guess we'll just cover what's 
left with student loans.

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:13.070
What's left?

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.050
What are you trying to do?

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.150
I guess it would be enough to send

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:19.190
Mutou-san and Sawaki to France.

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:21.920
What a waste of a harvest festival.

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:23.280
You said it.

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:25.380
That princess is such a pain.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.540
Whew, I'm so glad!

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:33.940
Kyokotan

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:33.940
It was a real battle with the 
gravure idol research society at the end.

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:37.420
So amazing! Pre-chewed 
sake by TanaKyo!

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:40.570
Hey, now, keep your voice down!

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:42.870
Anyway, I want to keep 
half of it forever,

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:44.950
but it would be pointless 
if it distills.

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:56.750
Final Event 
Venue

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:49.030
But I wish they'd send 
us that video clip, too!

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:50.360
I know!

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:52.380
There aren't even any clips of Kyokotan

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:53.980
putting something in 
her mouth on the DVDs!

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:55.050
Indeed.

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:56.960
Those guys sure are happy.

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:00.780
Bringing that pre-chewed sake 
to the final event...

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:03.140
They don't even realize 
that a celebrity's guards

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:04.340
aren't that easy.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:06.170
Ignorance is bliss, I guess.

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:11.480
78th Annual Harvest Festival Last              vent

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:09.510
I-It was fake?

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:10.920
Yeah, sort of.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.350
78th Annual Harvest Festival Last Night Event

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.950
Moyashimon

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.950
Episode 6

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe 
Theater

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe Theater Returns!

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:55.090 --> 00:21:58.270
Well, if it isn't the kyokai yeasts!

00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:02.240
We're a new variety of yeast

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:04.030
resulting from selective breeding!

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:06.050
Selective breeding?

00:22:06.460 --> 00:22:07.300
Yes!

00:22:07.300 --> 00:22:09.670
We've been bred selectively to produce

00:22:09.670 --> 00:22:13.320
the best yeasts for optimal 
flavor and fermentation!

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:14.420
Wow!

00:22:14.420 --> 00:22:17.220
But how does selective 
breeding work for microbes?

00:22:17.220 --> 00:22:18.650
Could it be...

00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:20.970
No!

00:22:20.970 --> 00:22:23.230
Please, don't!

00:22:25.470 --> 00:22:26.710
No, not like that!

00:22:26.710 --> 00:22:29.660
Selective breeding means 
that humans intentionally

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:32.490
create stress on us, 
leading to sudden variations.

00:22:35.590 --> 00:22:37.780
Like shining ultraviolet light on us...

00:22:40.590 --> 00:22:44.760
Or putting us in hot baths.

00:22:45.220 --> 00:22:47.900
It sure was rough...

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:50.710
You call that stress?
